-- tests-independent.l4: scenarios written from the text of ukpga-2006-46.txt (lines 10757-14665) BEFORE any module was opened; see ANSWERS.md.
-- Expected values are the test author's, never copied from the encoding's output.
-- JUST TRUE / JUST FALSE = the text answers yes / no; NOTHING = the text does not decide (the family's "not covered").

-- Helper: the longest prison term in months from a MAYBE Penalty (Years are turned into months), so that the expected value is the author's own reading of the text.
GIVEN pen IS A MAYBE Penalty
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`my months of imprisonment` MEANS
    CONSIDER pen
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST p THEN
        CONSIDER p's `imprisonment not exceeding`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
        WHEN JUST per THEN JUST (IF per's unit EQUALS Years THEN per's `number of units` TIMES 12 ELSE per's `number of units`)

-- Helper: does the fine in a MAYBE Penalty have a stated cap? JUST FALSE where the fine is "a fine without a stated limit".
GIVEN pen IS A MAYBE Penalty
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`my fine has a stated cap` MEANS
    CONSIDER pen
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST p THEN
        CONSIDER p's `fine not exceeding`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
        WHEN JUST f THEN
            CONSIDER f
            WHEN `a fine without a stated limit` THEN JUST FALSE
            OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- Helper: the longest prison term in months of the first penalty in a list (the list starts with conviction on indictment).
GIVEN pens IS A LIST OF Penalty
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`my first penalty in months` MEANS
    CONSIDER pens
    WHEN EMPTY THEN NOTHING
    WHEN p FOLLOWED BY rest THEN `my months of imprisonment` (JUST p)
