#ASSERT (`Under section 1040, may my company register under this Act as the kind of company I choose` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE `s 1040(3) as a company limited by guarantee`) EQUALS JUST FALSE -- S33-1 seat s1040(4)(b) L14636: a joint stock company limited by letters patent may not register as a company limited by guarantee
#ASSERT (`Under section 1043(1), does the section on unregistered companies apply to my body` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE -- S33-2 seat s1043(1) L14652: a UK body formed for gain, not exempt, not an OEIC
#ASSERT (`Under section 859K(7), what is the most I can be fined in pounds on summary conviction for that offence and for each day it continues` 1000) EQUALS (LIST (JUST 1000), (JUST 100)) -- S25-6 seat s859K(7) L11755: level 3 (taken as 1,000 pounds) and, for continued contravention, one-tenth of level 3 a day
#ASSERT (`Under section 860(5), what is the most my company can be fined in pounds on summary conviction for not registering its charge` 5000) EQUALS JUST 5000 -- S25-7 seat s860(5)(b) L11853: the statutory maximum (taken as 5,000 pounds)
#ASSERT (`Under section 998(4), what is the most I can be fined on summary conviction for an offence under section 998, in pounds` 1000) EQUALS JUST 1000 -- S30-6 seat s998(4) L13982: level 3 on summary conviction (taken as 1,000 pounds)
#ASSERT (`Under section 999(5), what is the most I can be fined on summary conviction for an offence under section 999, in pounds` 1000) EQUALS JUST 1000 -- S30-7 seat s999(5) L13993: level 3 on summary conviction (taken as 1,000 pounds), no daily default fine
